{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicNormalization","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicZAxisUniqueness"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hypMinimizerUnique_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hypMinimizerUnique_derived","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicUniqueness.lean#L128-L138","doc":"**`HypMinimizerUnique` is DERIVABLE** — the derived witness of the T2\ngeodesic-uniqueness conjecture, assembled from WALL-2 (`exists_normalization_isom`)\nand WALL-4 (`zaxis_minimizer_eq_vseg`) via `hyp_minimizer_unique_pointwise`.\n\nDeliberately a `def`, NOT a global `instance`: it does not auto-activate the\n`[HypMinimizerUnique]`-conditional theorems across the corpus.  Promotion to a\nglobal `instance` is the owner's call after reviewing the two supporting walls.\n`HyperbolicGeodesic` is left untouched (no fabricated instance there). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hyp_minimizer_unique_pointwise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hyp_minimizer_unique_pointwise","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicUniqueness.lean#L97-L126","doc":"**WALL-5 — geodesic uniqueness in `H³` (DERIVED, sorry-free).**  Between any two\npoints of `H³`, two constant-speed length-minimisers agree pointwise on `[0,1]`.\nThe reduction: normalise both endpoints onto the z-axis by an invertible\n`dH`-isometry `Φ` (WALL-2), where the two images `Φ∘γ`, `Φ∘δ` are minimisers\nbetween z-axis points, hence both equal the vertical segment (WALL-4); injectivity\nof `Φ` then transfers the equality back.\n\nThis is exactly the content of the open `HypMinimizerUnique.unique` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.minimizer_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.minimizer_comp","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicUniqueness.lean#L78-L95","doc":"**A `dH`-isometry maps a constant-speed minimiser to a constant-speed\nminimiser** (given that it preserves the distance between the endpoints).  All\nthree fields transport: admissibility by `admissiblePath_comp`, minimality by\n`pathLenH_comp` together with the endpoint-distance hypothesis `hdH`, and constant\nspeed by `speed_comp` (the line element is preserved pointwise). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zAxisPt_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zAxisPt_eq","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicUniqueness.lean#L67-L76","doc":"**A z-axis point equals `zpt` of its height.**  A point of `zAxis` has both\nhorizontal coordinates `0`, so it is `(0,0,·)` — the value `zpt ((·) 2)`.  Lets a\n`zAxis` membership be fed to the z-axis uniqueness lemma, which is stated in terms\nof `zpt`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}